 evaporation","little water vapor","heating increases the droplets"],"cool does not vapor water":["much water vapor","few droplets","cooling increases condensation"],"alternation comes from of rotation sphere":["the point marked enters and goes out from light","rotation changes the state","the source remains fixed"],"alternation comes from off source turning":["rotation is not necessary","the source turns off","all the points darkens simultaneously"],"comes from is lack layer of strong that too transport":["the water is fast-flowing","little deposition","the sediments appear farther downstream"],"comes fragments from lack lack layer of of":["the water may be slow-flowing","no deposits appear in the collector","no fragments are present"],"active is of pollution source still":["increases after discharge","level large near source","stopping the source reduces rapid the input new"],"in is old pollutant sediments":["increasing does not follow discharges new","level decreases slowly","the source is stopped"],"comes energy from lack little of portion satiety too with":["increasing the portion helps","energy below target","protein may be present"],"comes composition from lack unsuitable":["energy at target","the required component is missing","changing the composition helps"],"error is random unusual value":["the instrument passes the check","a alone measurement differs","the repeated measurements groups"],"instrument is misadjusted":["another instrument gives a different level","repetition keeps deviation","all the measurements are shifted"]}}

@slots literal
{
  "observation": "the observed problem exists, but its cause has not yet been located",
  "hypothesis1": "the lack of the layer comes from transport that is too strong",
  "hypothesis2": "the lack of the layer comes from a lack of fragments"
}

@answer jsEval
const probe = (condition, message) => { if (!condition) { throw new Error("probe failed: " + message); } };
const slots = $slots;
const facts = (typeof $facts === "object" && $facts !== null) ? $facts : JSON.parse(String($facts));
const key = (text) => String(text).toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, " ").trim().split(" ").filter((word) => word !== "" && word !== "the" && word !== "a" && word !== "an").sort().join(" ");
probe(typeof slots.observation === "string" && slots.observation.length > 0, "the statement must report the observation already made");
probe(typeof slots.hypothesis1 === "string" && slots.hypothesis1.length > 0, "the first hypothesis must carry its printed text");
probe(typeof slots.hypothesis2 === "string" && slots.hypothesis2.length > 0, "the second hypothesis must carry its printed text");
const table = facts.predictions;
probe(typeof table === "object" && table !== null && !Array.isArray(table), "the fact wire must carry the prediction table keyed by hypothesis");
probe(Object.keys(table).length > 0, "the prediction table must not be empty");
const predictions1 = table[key(slots.hypothesis1)];
const predictions2 = table[key(slots.hypothesis2)];
probe(Array.isArray(predictions1) && predictions1.length > 0, "the first hypothesis must have a prediction set in the fact table");
probe(Array.isArray(predictions2) && predictions2.length > 0, "the second hypothesis must have a prediction set in the fact table");
probe((predictions1.indexOf(slots.observation) !== -1) === (predictions2.indexOf(slots.observation) !== -1), "the observation already made must be compatible with both hypotheses");
const first = predictions1.find((prediction) => predictions2.indexOf(prediction) === -1);
const second = predictions2.find((prediction) => predictions1.indexOf(prediction) === -1);
probe(first !== undefined, "the first hypothesis must predict something the second does not");
probe(second !== undefined, "the second hypothesis must predict something the first does not");
return "We check “" + first + "” (or equivalently “" + second + "”), because the result separates the two hypotheses.";

